        },
        "text": "The algebra predicts a false removal: the replica can serve, but it leaves the EndpointSlice and the rules of each node. The band is 12 s to 24.105 s after the fault. The readiness check of the target fails for the hold (30 s), but its route still serves. Its latch trips 8 s–18 s after the fault. Then the controller of the service is not ready, thus the service refuses each request with a 503. The kubelet and the propagation (CAL.T07.iptables: median 0.059 s, 33 times) remove the target 12 s–24.105 s after the fault: a false removal. Each refusal closes its connection with a GOAWAY on its session, and the next request opens a new connection one turn (0.02 s) later. A chain of picks of the target ends at the first pick of the other replica. The target answers each stream at once, thus the session check closes no session, and D is the same as C. Each pick goes to the target at random, thus the failures of the 3 connections are negative binomial: 0–9 in 95 % of the runs. A chain longer than 11 picks has a chance of 0.001 at the most."
      },
